  "about": "Every NUMERIC key a provider's usage object has been seen to carry, by dotted path from the usage object (arrays are not walked). known_priced: PM turns it into money. known_info: PM reads or knowingly ignores it, and it never changes a price (it is already inside a priced count, or it is a count of something free). known_unpriced: PM cannot price it; a value above 0 makes the row 'at least', and the value is the closed cost_note slug. A numeric key in none of the three is a new token type. Non-numeric keys (service_tier, inference_geo, speed ...) and arrays (Gemini's promptTokensDetails, whose non-text modality is the slug non_text_prompt) are never walked, so slugs lists only the ones a key maps to. The Rust usage reader and the weekly provider canary read this one file.",
